cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, code, or the reported results, please cite the repository."
title: "ContextDAG: dependency-graph context management for multi-turn LLM conversations — benchmark and staged evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Leiva
    given-names: Christian
repository-code: "https://github.com/chleiva/ContextDAG"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
keywords:
  - large language models
  - conversational context
  - context management
  - retrieval
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  ContextDAG represents a multi-turn conversation as a dependency graph and builds model
  context from the branches a new message depends on. This repository contains the synthetic
  benchmark (145 annotated scenarios across 13 structural families, plus long-history
  variants), six context-construction methods, a staged evaluation (oracle feasibility,
  candidate realism, judge recalibration, retrieval comparability, length pilot, length
  ablation) with pre-registered thresholds, every LLM call's cost ledger, and the results.
